STEP 1 -- BL-NORM IMPLEMENTATION: PROVENANCE + BASELINE-WINDOW DEFINITION
==============================================================================
Implementations found in the repo (full reasoning in this file's module docstring):
  1. scripts/common.py :: bl_norm_labels(X, y, groups)
  2. 3_anxolotl/demographics_analysis.py :: baseline_relative_scale(X, y, groups)
  3. 3_anxolotl/window_size_ablation_no_phase3.py :: baseline_relative_scale(X, y, groups)
  4. 2_cross_dataset/cross_dataset_blnorm.py :: baseline_relative_scale(X, y, groups)   <-- USED HERE
  5. 3_anxolotl/_canonical_sensitivity_common.py :: baseline_relative_scale_capped(X, y, groups, cap=None)
  (rejected) scripts/common.py :: bl_norm_protocol / cross_dataset_blnorm.py :: baseline_relative_scale_protocol(X, groups, n_baseline=8) -- fixed-8-window, Anxolotl-protocol-only, label-agnostic. Wrong for WESAD (see below).

(1)-(4) are the SAME leak-fixed (2026-07-19) logic: per subject, leading run of y==0 windows (stops at first non-zero label), used as the mean/std reference for a per-feature z-score applied to that subject's entire timeline. (5) with cap=None reproduces this exactly.

CHOSEN: 2_cross_dataset/cross_dataset_blnorm.py :: baseline_relative_scale
  Reason: its own docstring states it is "used here for WESAD's training side" -- the only implementation with direct, documented WESAD provenance in this repo (the others were written for/used on Anxolotl). Functionally identical to (1)-(3), so this choice changes nothing numerically vs. picking one of those instead.

Baseline-window definition for WESAD (from 1_wesad/wesad_preprocessing.py line 14: "WESAD labels: 1->baseline(0), 2->stress(1), others->skip"): y==0 IS EXACTLY the WESAD protocol's Baseline condition -- amusement/meditation (other WESAD labels) are never included in this dataset at all, so there is no ambiguity about what counts as "baseline" here. Because baseline is a single continuous block at the START of every subject's recording (by protocol design) and no window is ever re-labelled 0 later, the "leading run of y==0" equals ALL of that subject's y==0 windows -- verified below.

